  "worked_solution": "The range of $\\sqrt[6]{x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[6]{x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches do not affect the range. Hence,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[6]{2-3x}\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-3,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{2-3x} & \\ge 0 \\\\ -3\\sqrt[6]{2-3x} & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of the given function is $f(x)\\in (-\\infty ,0].$\n\nWe can also see that this is true from the graph of the function. The graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14249143/assets/ce3b0c967ed01cfad58df6cf2c8f014d74dbde0e0438d401dcef04b2e359baa5.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
